## October 15 fully observed scorecard cohort

The separate scorecard covers **27 fully observed windows out of 79 eligible**; **52 are gap windows**. Of the complete cohort, 26 traded windows generated 124 fills and 167.83 matched pairs. Pair cost: **$1.0272**; cohort fees: **$0.3744**. Cohort P&L is **$-10.0028**: locked **$-4.5708**, directional **$-5.4320**. This differs from raw daily totals because it is a deliberately narrower fully observed population; do not add or substitute one for the other. The day is still open, `day_complete` is false, and the scorecard says full-day discovery/recording coverage is uncertified and some window coverage or fill history is missing or invalid.

## Where the recorded losses sit

In the fully observed October 15 cohort, both components are negative: **$4.5708 locked** and **$5.4320 directional**, with directional loss larger. In the raw October 15 aggregate, locked P&L is positive **$4.5012**, while directional P&L is negative **$9.5459** and larger in magnitude, producing the raw net loss. These are two different populations and neither supports attributing a cause to the strategy. In the scorecard, per-window results apply only to its observed sample; they do not represent missing windows or the whole day.

